+### Formatting Any Streamable Type
+
+The library now supports formatting any type that can be used with `std::cout <<`:
+
+```cpp
+// Format integers
+std::cout << Colorize(42, Color::Green) << std::endl;
+
+// Format booleans
+std::cout << Colorize(true, Color::Blue) << std::endl;
+
+// Format floating-point numbers
+std::cout << Colorize(3.14159, Color::Yellow) << std::endl;
+std::cout << Stylize(2.71828f, Style::Bold) << std::endl;
+
+// Format characters
+std::cout << Colorize('X', Color::Magenta) << std::endl;
+
+// Format with full options
+FormatOptions opts(Color::Red, Style::Bold);
+std::cout << Format(999, opts) << std::endl;
+```
+
+All functions (`Colorize`, `Stylize`, and `Format`) work with any type that supports the stream insertion operator (`<<`), including:
+- Integers (`int`, `long`, `short`, etc.)
+- Floating-point numbers (`float`, `double`)
+- Booleans (`bool`)
+- Characters (`char`)
+- Strings (`std::string`, `const char*`, `std::string_view`)
+- Any custom type with an overloaded `operator<<`
+
