 ### Functions
 
-- `Format(text, options)` - Format text with full options
-- `Colorize(text, color)` - Apply foreground color
-- `Stylize(text, style)` - Apply text style
+All formatting functions accept both string types and any type that supports stream insertion (`<<`):
+
+- `Format(value, options)` - Format any streamable value with full options
+  - `std::string Format(std::string_view text, const FormatOptions &options = {})`
+  - `template<Streamable T> std::string Format(const T &value, const FormatOptions &options = {})`
+  
+- `Colorize(value, color)` - Apply foreground color to any streamable value
+  - `std::string Colorize(std::string_view text, Color color)`
+  - `template<Streamable T> std::string Colorize(const T &value, Color color)`
+  
+- `Stylize(value, style)` - Apply text style to any streamable value
+  - `std::string Stylize(std::string_view text, Style style)`
+  - `template<Streamable T> std::string Stylize(const T &value, Style style)`
+
 - `Divider(symbol, width, options)` - Create divider line with custom symbol (runtime override)
 - `Divider(width, options)` - Create divider line with CMake-configured default symbol
 - `Sanitize(text)` - Remove control characters
 - `StripAnsi(text)` - Remove ANSI escape codes
 
+**Note**: The template versions work with any type that can be streamed to `std::ostream`, including integers, floats, booleans, characters, and custom types with overloaded `operator<<`.
+
 ### CMake Options
 
 - `CONMAT_DEFAULT_DIVIDER_SYMBOL` - Configure the default symbol for Divider function (default: "=")
